<span id="lstnumberx90" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx90.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span id="lstnumberx90.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[-37.6015000,</span><span id="lstnumberx90.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx90.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">145.0250000]]</span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Model Details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Linear</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reconstruct the masked segment by connecting the segment’s start and end GPS coordinates with a straight line and sampling evenly along that line.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Linear + HMM</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Produce a simple, connected candidate polyline via linear interpolation, then snap it to the road/path network using a standard HMM-based map-matching service. For this step, we call the OSRM’s HMM-based Map Matching API. The HMM combines (1) emission probabilities: likelihood of each observed point being near a road candidate (distance-based) and (2) transition probabilities: likelihood of moving between candidates given road graph connectivity and plausible travel costs; OSRM encapsulates this logic and returns a most-likely path (Viterbi).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">TrajFM</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adapt the pre‑trained TrajFM to GlobalTrace as a masked coordinate recovery model by aligning data, projection, and supervision to the task. Concretely, we keep the TrajFM
architecture fixed and load pre‑trained weights, then project trajectories into metric space using per‑group UTM coordinates with the correct zone. We convert GlobalTrace supervision into the model’s tokenized format using a task‑specific padder that masks only spatial features at indices flagged by the dataset’s mask column, and finetune with the following settings:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Hyperparameter</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Value</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Optimizer</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Adam (weight decay <math id="A5.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning rate</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A5.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Epochs</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Scheduler</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">CosineAnnealingLR (<math id="A5.T7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{max}}{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{max}}{=}20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}{=}1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}{=}1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Batch size</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">16</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Loss weights</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">spatial=2.0, temporal=0.5, token=0.5</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Gradient clipping</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">max_norm=1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T7.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T7.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Task/Padder</th>
<td id="A5.T7.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">gt_mask (masked coordinate recovery)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Finetuning hyperparameters for TrajFM</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
