<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Directional metrics: Large gap.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A clear pattern shown in <a href="#A8.T9" title="In H.1 Results for each reconstruction direction ‣ Appendix H Detailed results ‣ Understanding the Geospatial Reasoning Capabilities of LLMs: A Trajectory Recovery Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> to <a href="#A8.T11" title="In H.1 Results for each reconstruction direction ‣ Appendix H Detailed results ‣ Understanding the Geospatial Reasoning Capabilities of LLMs: A Trajectory Recovery Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> is that many LLMs show high GT→REC and much lower REC→GT (e.g., good coverage of the ground-truth path but poor precision). Interpreting the directions:
GT→REC measures recall (how much of the GT path is covered by the reconstruction), while REC→GT measures precision (how much of the reconstructed path lies on or near the GT). So a
low REC→GT alongside a high GT→REC typically means the model covers most of the true route but also adds extra, off-route geometry—spurs, loops, or side streets—so a large share of
reconstructed points are not close to the GT.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Activity results</h3>

<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show the activite bias results in <a href="#A8.T12" title="In H.2 Activity results ‣ Appendix H Detailed results ‣ Understanding the Geospatial Reasoning Capabilities of LLMs: A Trajectory Recovery Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T12" class="ltx_table">
<p id="A8.T12.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A8.T12.2.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:394.3pt;height:97.2pt;vertical-align:-46.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Model</span>
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">boat</span>
<span id="A8.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">bus</span>
